{"hash":"64b66fde6294ac86","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":79.953,"said":"You are on the porch now, before the low door of the sanctum. Feel how wet the floor is under your feet: everyone who comes here pours water, and Baba’s whole day is counted out in offerings. At four in the morning the doors open, and the first offering is the Kancha Jal, the first water of the day. Through the day pilgrims pour Ganga water and milk, and lay down bel leaves and flowers. In the evening the doors open again for the Shringar Puja, when the linga is adorned and the aarti is sung. Twice a year this temple becomes a wedding house. On Basant Panchami, devotees from Mithila, in north Bihar, arrive with their kanwars to offer the Tilak, the ceremony that begins a Hindu wedding, and so the season of Shiva’s marriage opens. Then on Mahashivratri, through the four watches of the night, sindoor, vermilion, is offered to Baba, marking the completion of his marriage to Parvati. That is why the red threads hang outside. Now bow your head; the doorway is low. Step inside with me, and carry your water the last few steps.\n\nDid you know? The temple is open from about four in the morning to nine at night, with a break in the afternoon; during the Shravani Mela the hours are extended.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1035},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1051,"end":1198}],"words":[[0.098,0.192,0,3],[0.302,0.132,4,7],[0.447,0.108,8,10],[0.567,0.084,11,14],[0.663,0.361,15,20],[1.036,0.349,21,24],[1.613,0.349,26,32],[1.973,0.072,33,36],[2.057,0.264,37,40],[2.334,0.264,41,45],[2.61,0.108,46,48],[2.73,0.096,49,52],[2.838,0.649,53,60],[4.399,0.312,62,66],[4.724,0.24,67,70],[4.976,0.204,71,74],[5.192,0.108,75,78],[5.312,0.373,79,84],[5.697,0.132,85,87],[5.841,0.216,88,93],[6.07,0.144,94,98],[6.226,0.421,99,103],[6.983,0.541,105,113],[7.536,0.096,114,117],[7.644,0.349,118,123],[8.005,0.276,124,128],[8.293,0.288,129,134],[8.594,0.481,135,140],[9.267,0.192,142,145],[9.471,0.